WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.501
I've always loved seeing you.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:04.968
And I want to talk about the --
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:07.868
-Oh, come on. The series --
-Hello? Is this real?

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.734
-No, this is chocolate.
It's cake.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:12.868
"Is it cake?"
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.200
"Is it cake."
-Yeah, yeah. Thank you.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.234
-Oh, yeah.
I want to talk to you about,

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:18.934
obviously, the success of
"Better Things."

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:22.667
The series finale.
Listen to some of these reviews.

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:25.100
"Hollywood Reporter" --
very important.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.701
They say, "The fifth season of
'Better Things'

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:30.200
is the best TV show of the year
thus far.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.267
This show impacts the way
I see everything around me."

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.767
-April.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.133
-That's "Hollywood Reporter."
"Variety" says,

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.434
"the final season of
'Better Things'

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:39.167
is a moment of change for TV."

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.501
"Time" magazine, "The final
season of 'Better Things'

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:44.033
is Pamela Adlon's masterpiece."

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.267
And right now it's 100% fresh
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.968
Ladies and gentlemen...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.701
...what more can I say?
What more can I say

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.801
about "Better Things"
except it doesn't get better?

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.767
-Thank you.
-And then the podcast --

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.434
-Yeah. Yes.
-If you like podcasts,

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.434
listen to
the "Better Things" podcast.

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.734
-Yes. We have a compan--
I wanted to do it.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:05.067
I wanted to be like other people
and, like, real TV shows.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:09.367
So, I was like, "Let me do --
Let me do what these people

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.200
are doing.
Like, a companion --"

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.601
So I talk about
the whole season,

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:16.234
but then I have, like,
a different person on.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:19.767
And so, like,
I just had Cree Summer.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.501
She just did
the last one with me.

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:24.801
And we talked about
being O.G. voiceover people.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:28.434
And we do, like, deep dives.
And then after the show's over,

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:30.968
I'm gonna keep the podcast going
because I want to be like

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:34.300
Huell Howser, basically,
or Mister Rogers, so...

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.834
-But you recently just
told the story about how you

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.534
filmed this season, of course,
during the pandemic,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.334
and this is
when it was tough to film.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.100
You actually filmed
a lot of it in London.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.167
-Yes, we had to because --

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.267
So, Celia Imrie,
who plays my mom...

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:52.701
-Amazing.
-...she doesn't fly,

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.267
historically, and it's not
because she's a diva.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:57.801
She has a heart --
-Okay, a medical condition.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:59.367
-A medical reason.
-Sure.

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:04.067
-And so she would take, like,
the QE2 every year,

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:07.067
like the "Yentl,"
"Papa, watch me fly," like,

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.501
on the front of the boat.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.234
But they weren't
booking passengers.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:13.367
-The "Yentl" --
-Thank you.

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.767
-Oh, my gosh.
-Thank you.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.701
-That is so funny.
-I knew you would know.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:19.767
-Barbra Streisand, love it.
-Yeah, and so, they weren't

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.968
booking passage
because of COVID this year.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.400
And I'm like,
"I can't do a whole season --"

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.901
Because it's three generations
of women on my show,

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:29.367
and I can't have Phyl,
like, on Zoom.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:33.601
So, we -- I mean,
we went through everything.

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.801
FX, my network,
at one point, they were like,

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:37.934
"We found a boat.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:40.334
It costs a million dollars."

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.334
And I was like, "What?"
-"Yeah, we --"

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:44.701
-"You're gonna
put the old lady on the boat?

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.367
Can it go mid-Atlantic?
Like, is that safe?"

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.767
-No, this is
a terrible thing to do.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.968
-So, then,
we just eventually figured out

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:53.801
how to shoot her scenes
all in England.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.334
So, any time you see Phyl
this season,

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.601
we're in England with her.
-Wow!

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:00.834
And the magic of -- and
they just made it look like --

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.100
-And beautiful.
-Seamless.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.467
-My production designers,
the art department,

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:07.734
everybody worked so hard.
They were incredible.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.901
-I love the music in the show,

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.901
and I know, this season,

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.734
you start off
with a little "Monty Python."

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:15.968
-I thought, you know,
because people said,

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.667
"Are you gonna
address COVID in the show?"

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.467
And I went through all these
kind of machinations,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.501
and I thought, "Maybe we'll
do it in flashbacks."

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:26.467
And I'm like, "No, it's still
going to be around."

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.167
Because, I remember, I was here

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:30.868
like two nights before
everything got shut down.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.000
-I remember this.
-Remember?

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.801
I had the thieves spray.
-I do remember that.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:37.067
-I wouldn't shake your hand, but
I shook Rachel Maddow's hand.

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.067
-You basically --
You hugged Rachel --

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.367
[ Laughter ]
-I licked her.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.167
-You hugged Rachel Maddow.
-I was like, "No, bro!"

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.400
-Yeah, you're like,
"Jimmy, chill, man."

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.701
-Yes, exactly.
-And then, "Rachel Maddow, hi!"

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:48.501
And I go, "Hey. What am I?"
I watched it happen.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:52.033
Yes.
-So, I wanted to come back

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:55.901
with hearing Eric Idle
start the song.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.167
-What does he say again?
-He says,

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:01.100
"Whenever life gets you down,
Mrs. Brown,

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.734
and things seem hard or tough
and people are stupid,

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:10.234
obnoxious, or daft, and you feel
like you've had quite enough,

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:13.767
just remember that you're
standing on a planet

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.334
that's evolve -- evolving."
Yeah.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:19.000
I don't want to --
It's Eric Idle. It's not --

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.167
-No, that's brilliant.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.400
-But it's about the bigness
of the universe.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.067
And it's like...
-How small we actually are.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:27.434
-...how small we are.
And it's just, you know,

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:31.067
that people get really --

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.968
Like, everything's
really messed up right now,

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:38.367
and we can feel really bad,
but there are so many

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.067
good things happening,
and you can't sit there and go,

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.901
"I can't help this,
I can't help that,

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.501
so I'm not gonna help anything."

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.801
Pick a thing.
Pick a thing.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:49.100
-Yeah.
-And then you can make a change.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.701
-Yeah.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.734
That's exactly the vibe.
That's what I want.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:57.334
I'm gonna be sad to see it go,
but this is your baby.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.501
I mean, you put a lot of
your life into this.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.634
-Yeah, I am grateful.
-Heart and soul and sweat.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.100
Yeah, well done.
-Thank you.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.234
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.200
Here's Pamela Adlon
in "Better Things."

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.367
Take a look.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:09.334
-My head is spinning.

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:10.901
-I'll get you some crackers.

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.000
-Oof.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.601
Phyl...
-Hmm?

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:17.200
-Mom, let's take a picture.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.434
We hardly have any good pictures
on this trip together.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.033
-Absolutely not.

00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:24.334
My hair.
-Come here.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.334
-Don't grab me.
I'm not the cat's litter.

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.501
-One sec.
I love these stairs.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:31.067
Just one cool --

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:33.501
Just stand still.
-I've told you many times,

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.334
I don't like
a hand on my shoulder.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.901
-I want one cool selfie.

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:40.167
[ Body thudding ]
Aah!

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.901
Ohh!
-Sam?

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.767
-Pamela Adlon, everybody.
The final episode

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.367
of "Better Things"
airs next Monday

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:51.467
at 10:00 p.m. on FX and Hulu.
-Thank you.

